| Real-Time Latency | < 100ms | Per 100 tokens processed |

## Common Phase 6 Issues & Resolutions

| Issue | Resolution |
|-------|------------|
| Noise stripping removes error messages | Use `--entity-types error,warning` to limit NER classification to critical entities |
| Real-time filtering too slow | Enable GPU acceleration: `--onnx-providers cuda`, reduce batch size: `--batch-size 25` |
| ANSI stripping removes valid terminal control codes | Use `--ansi-patterns whitelist` to preserve specific essential codes |
| Noise profiles don't match agent type | Use `--agent-profile claude_code` or appropriate agent profile |
| Real-time latency > 100ms | Increase batch size: `--batch-size 100`, enable ONNX: `--onnx-providers cuda,cpu,auto` |
| Entropy analysis misclassifies important content | Adjust threshold: `--entropy-threshold 3.5` (increase) or `--entropy-threshold 2.5` (decrease) |
| Too much or too little stripping | Review agent noise profile: `draco noise --profile --show --agent claude_code` |

## Integration with Other Phases

### Phase 6 → Phase 1
- Noise cancellation results feed into baseline metrics update
- Reduction percentages from Phase 6 adjust Phase 1 reduction targets
- Quality preservation scores become part of Phase 1 quality baselines

### Phase 6 → Phase 2
- Cleaned terminal output feeds into zero-LLM routing (cleaner input = better pattern matching)
- Reduced noise improves deterministic command identification accuracy
- Reduction percentages combine: zero-LLM (40%) + noise cancellation (70%) = cumulative effect

### Phase 6 → Phase 3
- Cleaned terminal output provides cleaner input for Tree-sitter skeleton extraction
- Reduced noise improves AST parsing accuracy
- Reduction percentages combine: skeleton (40-50%) + noise cancellation (70%) = cumulative

### Phase 6 → Phase 4
- Cleaned context improves BM25 keyword indexing (fewer stop words, more important terms)
- Reduced noise improves ONNX semantic similarity scoring
- Reduction percentages combine: RAG (60-70%) + noise cancellation (70%) = diminishing returns but cumulative

### Phase 6 → Phase 5
- Cleaned terminal output provides better input for YAML filter training (fewer noise tokens)
- NER classifications inform YAML filter exclude/include patterns
- Agent-specific noise profiles configure agent-specific YAML filter rules

### Phase 6 → Phase 7
- Cleaned terminal output provides better input for transformer summarization (fewer noise tokens)
- NER classifications inform verdict generation conditioning
- Reduction percentages combine: verdict formatting (60-70%) + noise cancellation (70%) = optimized pipeline

### Phase 6 → Phase 9
- Cleaned code provides fewer tokens for model-aware pruning and quantization
- NER-identified important elements (error messages, etc.) are preserved through pruning
- Reduction percentages combine: pruning (40-50%) + noise cancellation (70%) = carefully orchestrated

## Skill Execution

### Command Line
```bash
# Initialize DraCo with Phase 6 Noise Cancellation
draco init --phase 6

# Classify terminal output entities
draco noise --classify --spaCy --entities 20 --input ./terminal_output.txt

# Strip ANSI codes
draco noise --strip-ansi --normalize --input ./terminal_output.txt --output ./cleaned.txt

# Detect and strip repetitive patterns
draco noise --detect-repetitive --strip --input ./terminal_output.txt --output ./cleaned.txt

# Run entropy analysis
draco noise --entropy-analysis --threshold 3.0 --input ./terminal_output.txt

# Apply agent-specific noise profile
draco noise --agent-profile claude_code --apply --input ./terminal_output.txt --output ./cleaned.txt

# Real-time filtering mode
draco noise --real-time --pipeline --latency 100ms --input ./streaming_terminal.txt

# View noise statistics
draco noise --stats --input ./terminal_output.txt
```

### Skill File Integration
This skill file is auto-loaded by DraCo at session start and integrates with:
- `.claude/skills/draco-baseline.skill` (Phase 1 - baseline for noise pattern identification)
- `.claude/skills/draco-mcp-integration.skill` (Phase 2 - cleaned output feeds zero-LLM routing)
- `.claude/skills/draco-tree-sitter.skill` (Phase 3 - cleaned output for skeleton extraction)
- `.claude/skills/draco-agent-hooks.skill` (Phase 10 - per-agent noise profile configurations)

### Dependencies
- Requires: `spaCy >= 3.7.0`, `spacy-model-en-core-web-sm >= 3.7.0`
- Requires: `draco-core >= 1.0`, `draco-nlp >= 1.0`
- Optional: `fuzzywuzzy >= 0.18.0` (for fuzzy pattern matching)
- Compatible with: All 50+ DraCo agent integrations

